      "defect_type": "Type I",
      "severity": 1,
      "explanation": "The proposal places a notification and review gate before a covered activity, but the available record does not show that this sequencing itself defeats later review.",
      "evidence": [],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask EPA to explain how the 90-day timing interacts with ongoing-use, cutoff-date, and emergency or low-volume provisions."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "evidence_to_intrusion_mismatch",
      "flaw_name": "Evidence-to-Intrusion Mismatch",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The proposed pre-commencement gate is supported at a general level by prior Orders, but the supplied packet does not provide enough chemical-specific evidence to test whether each designated use warrants the same control.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "II.A; II.B.1; Unit III",
          "quote_or_absence": "The notice states that EPA considered toxicity, exposure, releases, volume, and disposal, but the complete underlying TSCA Orders and technical evidence are not included in the supplied packet."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask EPA to publish a chemical-by-chemical evidence and Order crosswalk for every proposed significant new use."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "remedy_rationale_mismatch",
      "flaw_name": "Remedy-Rationale Mismatch",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The notice gives a general rationale for following Orders with SNURs, but the supplied record does not show why the same regulatory architecture is necessary and proportionate for every covered substance and activity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "II.B.1",
          "quote_or_absence": "The notice says it is necessary to follow a TSCA order with a SNUR, but the supplied packet does not include the Order-by-Order explanation supporting that generalization."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask EPA to compare the proposed common framework with chemical-specific or phased alternatives and explain the choice for each substance."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "implementation_fantasy",
      "flaw_name": "Implementation Fantasy",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The mechanism depends on market participants identifying confidential, Order-derived boundaries and completing a multi-part submission process, while operational examples and timing details are limited in the supplied record.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "II.C; II.D; II.F",
          "quote_or_absence": "The notice provides a bona fide-intent procedure for confidential uses, but the supplied packet does not explain how ordinary non-party firms can screen their activities before that procedure is invoked."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask EPA to provide screening examples, decision timelines, and implementation guidance for importers, processors, mixtures, articles, and borderline uses."
    },
